# `npm run dev:prod` — local Vite dev server (HMR, your working tree) against the PRODUCTION
# backend on cloud.pix3.dev. Live data: you are logged into the real account and editing real
# cloud projects.
#
# Why the proxy and not a direct cross-origin call: `import.meta.env.DEV` stays true in this mode
# (only `--mode production` flips it), so `/api`, `/collaboration` and `/preview` are requested
# same-origin and Vite's dev proxy forwards them to the target below. That buys two things the
# browser would otherwise refuse — no CORS preflight, and the auth cookie survives: the collab
# server sets it without a `Domain` attribute, so through the proxy it is scoped to
# `localhost:8123`, and Chrome accepts a `Secure; SameSite=None` cookie on `http://localhost`
# because localhost counts as a secure context.
#
# Room sockets are the one exception — `wsUrl` comes back from the fabric as an absolute
# `wss://rooms.pix3.dev/ws` and is opened directly, carrying `Origin: http://localhost:8123`.
# That origin must be listed in the fabric's `Rooms:Auth:AllowedOrigins` or the upgrade is
# rejected (see pix3-rooms `appsettings.Production.json`).
VITE_COLLAB_SERVER_URL=https://cloud.pix3.dev
